WEBVTT

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:03.560
Five, four, three,

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.770
<b>Western Japan</b>

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.430
two, one...

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.780
<i>When no one else is there,</i>

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.240
<i>you can count on Unit 9!</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>Unit 9</b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.070
<i>Leave West Japan to us!</i>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.490
<i>Unit 9 is justice!</i>

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.150
<i>Please recommend us to your friends.</i>

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:32.140
<i>Osaka's newly established Third Mobile 
Assault Unit 9, also known as "Unit 9,"</i>

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.550
<i>has become a very hard-working department, 
covering all of Western Japan.</i>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.720
<i>How does it feel to be the young, 
elite member leading Unit 9?</i>

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.180
<i>Inspector Kazari?</i>

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.330
<i>Well, I'm the only person in 
all of the police force</i>

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.690
<i>qualified to do this job.</i>

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.580
<i>I work with the knowledge that 
Japan's safety rests on my shoulders.</i>

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.360
<i>Everyone, please give me your 
cooperation and understanding.</i>

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.100
She's really gotten her act together.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:01.020
<i>We know your accomplishments in Unit 8 
led to your appointment as Unit 9's chief,</i>

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.030
No, she's getting way too cocky.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.720
<i>but how is it in Unit 9?</i>

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.080
<i>Wonderful.</i>

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.750
<i>My subordinates and I graduated the police 
academy at the top of our classes.</i>

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:13.410
<i>I believe we are equal, 
if not superior, to Unit 8.</i>

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.170
<i>Please give us your catchphrase.</i>

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.010
<i>We of Unit 9 will keep West Japan safe!</i>

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:20.280
<i>There you go!</i>

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.500
<i>Today's "Interview with the Elite" 
was with Kazari Asami,</i>

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.270
<i>leader of the West Japan ACTIVE project!</i>

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>Now for a fashion update!</i>

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.560
<i>Do you know what new material</i>

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.750
<i>is coming out of Shinyurigaoka?</i>

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.570
<i>You want to know, right?</i>

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.420
<i>Hear the answer after the break!</i>

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.530
<i>Everyone, come and miracle!</i>

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.920
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.450
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:52.380
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:58.720
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.960
<b>File 3: Angel and God of Destruction</b>

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.520
Brain, it's Fingers.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.020
Action preparations complete.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.210
Fingers, this is Brain.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.230
Action. Formation 9.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.460
Wait!

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.690
Fingers 1 and 3, protect me!

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.840
Yes, Brai—

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.430
Disable sublimation engine!

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.860
<i>Spinning Rush Ether!</i>

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:15.060
Jeez, how long will you act like rookies?!

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:33.020
The Fingers must be constantly 
aware of each other's positions.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.700
I've told you this.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.000
Why can't you do it?

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.780
Tomigusuku always falls behind.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.630
It's Kanna who falls behind!

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.380
Officer Nawa is too early!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.970
Sousuke's out of sync.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.510
It's Shimazakura's fault.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.130
Brain-chan,

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.560
I think you should begin with 
teamwork development.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.730
No need for that.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.410
Everyone, who's the center?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.190
Just think about the center!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.940
I'm sorry, Brain,

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.840
but in an ever-changing combat zone,

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.380
it's important for everyone to make decisions.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.360
We're trying to do what we think of as "justice."

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.900
Excuse me? Justice?!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.310
I'll tell you something.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.620
No one needs your justice!

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.450
I am justice here.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:19.680
Just shut up and do as I say!

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.550
If you get it, answer me!

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.510
Y-Yes, Brain!

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.940
I'll be a better boss than you, for sure.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.080
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.520
Yes, this is Kazari Asami.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.810
It's been a long time. We're doing...

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:58.540
Huh?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.040
A-Asami-chan...

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.840
Help me...

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.310
Great, what's going on?

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.200
I'm going to die!

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:08.900
Great?!

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:09.520
Brain!

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.690
Message from police HQ!

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:14.030
Unit 8 is requesting Unit 9's help!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.820
How could this happen,

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.600
at a time like this?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.410
Vitals, all green. Lock.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.910
A request for help?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.890
What happened?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.330
I'm only told that it's some kind of emergency.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.920
<b>Connection Approved</b>

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.500
Approvals complete.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.000
Security Bureau HQ, Special 
Public Safety Fifth Section,

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.340
Third Mobile Assault Unit 9,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.170
heading out!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.190
Roger!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.840
<b>Osaka Castle Park Station</b>

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:57.140
<i>All lines on the Osaka Loop will now be closed</i>

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.140
<b>All Lines Closed for Emergency Purposes</b>

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.030
<i>to allow an emergency train launch.</i>

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:02.730
<i>We apologize to all passengers 
for the disruption.</i>

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.150
There's no time to waste.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.350
Our top priority is getting there fast.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:09.310
There will be significant shock 
on impact, so be careful.

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.110
Kyoukai-sama, we'll count on you for support.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.570
I know, Brain-chan.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:26.800
<b>Osaka Catapult</b>

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.470
Osaka catapult set.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.050
Launch!

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.470
Fingers, this is Brain.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.130
It will be an hour until arrival.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.170
Do your best.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.340
Brain-chan, incoming message from Unit 8.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.650
Connecting.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.030
Hey, Kazari-kun, it's been so long.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.840
Funasaka-san, what's going on in Tokyo?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.210
Where's everyone in Unit 8?

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.960
We're in big trouble.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.610
A crime is happening,

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.750
and everyone's out with the flu 
except Kyoukai-san and me.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.910
The flu?!

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:05.040
We don't have nearly enough 
people, so this is a big help.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.700
Take care. No need to hurry.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:11.470
Y-You should have told me that before!

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.180
That's so mean!

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:21.140
The Osaka catapult takes a 
ton of money and strength!

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:29.260
You should have told me you were all sick,

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.350
or at least sent an e-mail!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.940
Sorry... I tried to tell you,

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.160
but I passed out.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:38.820
I really am sorry.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:41.230
I tried to send a message via public safety,

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:44.320
but the details were treated 
as classified information.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.260
Of course they were!

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.510
If Unit 8 is out,

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:52.510
who will protect Eastern Japan, 
especially the capital?

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:55.410
You guys are Unit 9's senpai,

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.460
so act like it!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.140
Asami!

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.090
Y-Yes...

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:00.800
Sorry.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:01.990
Thanks.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:02.730
Okay...

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.460
I'll take you out to lunch or something.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:08.940
If there are any sweets you want,
let me know later.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.900
Oh, Sena-san, aren't you a civilian now?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.560
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.510
I hope you don't mind.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.600
Then if I accept something from 
you, it might be bribery.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.570
So I respectfully decline, President.

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:22.220
Huh?

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.600
Um, hello.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.020
I'm honored to meet the one known

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.520
as the most elite member of 
the police since its inception,

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:32.570
even in this form.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.300
She seems kind of scary.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.680
Oh, you two haven't met her yet.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.600
Listen, between you and me, she...

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.110
What? Really?

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.850
And what's more, she...

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.410
Who are these girls?

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.960
Emilia Adelman-kun and Kaburagi Marimo-kun,

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.670
two new members.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.240
Both are highly talented.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.280
So newer than me?

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.700
So what's the incident?

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.530
Oh, this.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.780
C & D, a recording studio in Suginami.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:09.880
It's used primarily for dubbing 
anime and foreign movies.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.950
The criminals have taken it over

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:16.880
and issued a series of demands to 
all video production companies.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.470
<b>Our Souls Cry Out 

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.430
Huh?

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.930
You know how long it's been common

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:27.640
for movies to suddenly switch to using 
famous celebrities for Japanese dubs?

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.430
This is probably for PR purposes,

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:35.020
but popularity doesn't necessarily 
equal acting talent,

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:38.320
so I suppose they just can't accept it.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.990
Well, I do understand how they feel.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:45.170
Th-They're holed up over that?

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.200
I don't know if they're confident

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.310
that they can escape, or don't
care if they're captured.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:53.210
But the criminals are more 
serious than we'd thought.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.900
In addition to the Willwear on the roof,

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:23.340
many bombs that respond to sound 
are around the building.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.340
All citizens in a one-kilometer 
radius have been evacuated,

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.910
but the police can't get close.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.790
We'll try to ID the criminals,

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:35.620
as well as where they got their weapons, but—

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:36.990
No, there's no need!

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.000
President, you're a civilian now, 
so don't force yourself.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.880
I will stand in for the chief and 
handle the investigation.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.010
Now, come in, everyone!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.840
Shimazakura Yuyuko.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:51.100
Tomigusuku Aki.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.220
Miyoshi Kanna.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:53.290
Nawa Taiga.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:54.650
Torigoe Sousuke.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.110
These five are...

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.320
The fingers, and we exist for the brain!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.010
If you think we're stupid,

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:09.160
then making amateurs do dubbing is stupider!

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:12.000
Not only do they ruin top-quality movies,

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.540
but they steal work from true actors! 
What could be stupider?

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.400
We'll show them

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.300
the depth of our rage!

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:36.730
<b>Suginami Building Incident Response HQ 

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:31.260
Three vital signs detected in the 
building and surrounding area.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:34.440
There's been no trace of communications 
or attempts to contact the outside,

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.730
so we can assume they're just three.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:41.080
The problem is the sound-detecting 
bombs around the building.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:43.320
We don't know where they are or how many.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.200
Kyoukai-sama!

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:48.410
Oh, Kyoukai-kun.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:53.220
We're having the Association analyze the 
bomb we recovered for its specs.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.720
Any options?

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:55.870
Yes, Brain!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.980
I'm the leader, so you should use my plan!

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.450
Who are you calling the leader? 
I'm the real leader!

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.820
Get lost, self-proclaimed leader.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.680
More importantly, Brain, as the 
original leader, I have a plan.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.510
I'm the prime leader!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.790
I'm really not sure what to 
say about your troops.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.490
S-Sorry.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.980
I'll teach them a lesson later.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:20.360
So in the end, she tried all of their plans?

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:24.760
All were bold plans, and quite interesting, but...

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:26.130
But?

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.490
Ultra long-range sniping failed

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.160
when they shot the sniper first.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.250
The air assault above the building

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:37.790
was noticed and shot down.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.840
They tried to enter from below,

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.800
but there were bombs there, too.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:48.840
So they tried to silently sneak up, but...

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:52.810
Of course, they couldn't beat 
a criminal in Willwear.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:57.050
The plot to psychologically damage 
them with laser sights

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.310
just barely succeeded, but...

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:03.610
That's just being a jerk, isn't it?

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:06.780
I'm sorry!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:08.430
All these failures are

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:11.090
my responsibility as the acting chair.

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.200
Now, now...

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:17.190
We should resolve this before we 
worry about responsibility.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:18.990
Every day,

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:21.840
their demands gain

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.710
more sympathy on the Internet.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:25.420
<b>Idiot celebrities ruin movies with their crap voice acting 

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:25.880
<b>Idiot celebrities ruin movies with their crap voice acting 

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:26.670
<b>Idiot celebrities ruin movies with their crap voice acting 

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.090
<b>Idiot celebrities ruin movies with their crap voice acting 

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:30.470
If we can't resolve this, it'll turn into a mess.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.150
I should help, too—

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.950
Shut up, you little shit!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.310
I was a fool for giving the new kids a chance.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:40.220
I'll solve this immediately.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:46.490
The bombs the criminals are using 
contain two kinds of sensors.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.660
One responds to any sound over seventy decibels.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:53.890
The other responds to any sound 
in the human vocal range.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:57.620
It can also pick up anything from 
a cellphone or earphone.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:01.330
We can't make loud noises or 
use our communications.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:05.100
They're all set to not detonate simultaneously.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.820
And the vocal-detection sensors

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:11.340
are set to not respond to a certain range.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.890
That's right... If they responded 
to all frequencies,

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.890
even the criminals couldn't talk.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:18.690
Right.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:23.010
So we tried to determine 
the allowable range, and...

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.550
<i>Everyone, come and miracle!</i>

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.590
I've heard this voice somewhere before.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:30.420
Oh, did you forget?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:31.740
It's her.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:34.700
<i>Hello, everyone! It's Shinmei Amu!</i>

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.290
Amu-chan?

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:41.500
Yes. They're using voice changers to 
change their voices into this one.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.030
<i>Search complete!</i>

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:45.210
<i>I think this is the news you're looking for, Uncle.</i>

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.560
"Uncle"?

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:48.320
Thank you, Liko-chan.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.300
What?

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.430
That's what you're into?

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.640
<b>VA Switch! Heroine of Popular Foreign Drama <i>The Last Fleet</i> 
Changed From Shinmei Amu to Susan Antonko</b>

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:56.600
Shinmei Amu is a well-received 
actress who's done dubbing

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:59.470
for this foreign drama since the first episode.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:04.350
Oh, so they're changing to 
a new idol next season?

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:08.990
Her agency's pushing her, 
but her reputation is pretty bad.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:10.290
I understand.

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:13.060
I can see what started this.

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:14.450
But...

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:15.220
Yeah.

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:18.620
It's not the information you 
need to really end this.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.450
What will you do, Brain-chan?

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.290
There's no time left...

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:31.550
Everyone, care for some snacks and a break?

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.340
Funasaka-san, I need a favor.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.300
All right.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:38.010
Explanation's over.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.930
No questions.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:41.480
My orders are absolute!

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:42.390
Got it?

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.310
Yes, Brain!

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:44.850
I am Justice!

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:46.480
Yes, Brain!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:47.730
Justice is me!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.240
Yes, Brain!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:54.700
Did you see the news?

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.910
People are starting to support us.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.880
If enough people start backing us,

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:02.600
the company will have to stop 
pretending they don't see it.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.910
Once public opinion changes,

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.500
we take the route they prepared and run.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.340
Just wait, Amu-chan!

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:11.960
We'll bring back your angel's voice!

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:15.010
But is it okay to trust them?

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.400
This method's a Logos...

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:27.690
What are they trying to do?

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:41.210
<i>The bad guy has appeared!</i>

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.290
Wh-What?!

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:45.010
<i>He wrecks the town and causes chaos.</i>

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:50.560
<i>No one can stop him.</i>

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:58.050
<i>No! That's not true! We have him!</i>

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.590
Are they insane? What are they thinking?

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:02.350
<i>Iron legs and fists of steel!</i>

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:06.810
<i>His roaring drill is on our side!</i>

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.310
I'm sorry, boss!

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:12.440
I just thought Kazari-kun wanted to learn

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.530
the song for a New Year's party!

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.010
No...

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.850
No one would normally think of this plan.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:21.170
That's right.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:24.640
I understand the idea of detonating the bombs,

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:28.960
since we don't know their 
numbers or locations, but...

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.370
But normally, you wouldn't do it.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.440
This is a residential district.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.510
Who has to pay for this?

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.730
Has she gotten worse?

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:41.470
I think this is who she always really was.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:45.430
<i>My song is destroying everyone's city...</i>

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:50.190
That got rid of all the bombs, right?

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:52.650
That's why you're a failure of a human.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:55.690
Just in case, everyone change your voice mode.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:56.960
Yes, Brain.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:00.890
Security Bureau HQ, Special 
Public Safety Fifth Section,

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:04.170
Third Mobile Assault Unit 9, heading out!

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:05.200
Heading out!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.530
You can't screw with us!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:17.510
Wh-Where did they go?

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.180
Too slow!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.030
Formation 9!

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:28.810
Roger!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:32.740
Take this!

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:39.360
Gotcha!

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.300
N-No...

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.870
They just ran in without thinking of the damage...

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:49.160
<b>Activate?</b>

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:48.710
<i>In the end, I want to hear your voice!</i>

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:00.230
I told you there was a chance the criminal

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:04.110
would self-destruct and that you 
need to be prepared for it.

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:05.600
You're slacking off.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.440
Splendid.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.310
That was a little too flashy, though.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:13.900
Well, as long as they were able

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.360
to protect the town.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.260
Get inside the police's patrol car.

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.610
Everyone's waiting.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.660
That voice... A-Amu-chan?

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.330
I changed my voice, just like you did.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:31.940
Brain, since we all have this voice, 
let's do that thing to finish it!

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:34.510
Yeah, we all talked about it.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:35.390
That thing?

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:36.560
That thing!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.050
Well, okay.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:40.920
All right, let's go.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.260
Everyone...

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.110
No...

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:43.720
Don't.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:44.930
Miracle!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.340
I see...

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.770
I can see why she's nicknamed
the "God of Destruction."

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:58.050
She truly is a legendary police officer.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:01.800
Yes, she's the officer who's written the most

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:04.880
letters of apology in police force history.

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.140
I don't come even close.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:08.880
She truly is great.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:11.310
You don't think she's just getting worse?

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:15.460
She really did get the worst parts 
of both Kuroki-san and Sena-san.

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.160
She did not!

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:23.450
We had no idea that Shinmei Amu's catchphrase

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:26.190
was the bomb's activation frequency.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:28.090
I'm sorry.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:30.100
Did you know that

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.280
Shinmei Amu left the show not because 
the company asked her to,

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.750
but for her own reasons?

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.920
Yes, I saw the story in the media this morning.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:40.360
<b>Breaking News 

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.510
I have a high opinion of you,

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:47.200
but I want you to understand that 
I can't cover for you forever.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:50.440
Yes, I'm terribly sorry.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:55.040
And about what Yamabuki-kun 
and Kuroki-kun said to me...

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.400
Permission should be granted.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:58.630
Thank you.

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:00.520
And with this incident, too?

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:03.550
Yes, they may be involved.

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:06.250
He is a permanent surveillance target.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:09.330
If Kuroki-kun becomes his guardian,

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:10.650
then if something happens,

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.800
I want you to be aware that it will 
be a problem for all of Unit 8.

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:15.540
We're aware.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.030
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:53.530
Ohakonyapachininko! It's Shinmei Amu!

00:23:52.360 --> 00:24:04.910
File 4: Mythos, Once More

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:55.760
Except it's actually Kazari Asami.

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:58.250
Not bad, Kazari-kun. That was identical.

00:23:58.250 --> 00:24:00.040
Really? That makes me happy.

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:01.090
More importantly, what's next?

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:04.390
The next episode is, um... Jirou-kun does a lot!

00:24:04.390 --> 00:24:04.890
Who?
